From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 13:41:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: apple: t8132-j604: hold the scaler's PMP
 request while the AVD decodes

macOS 26B123 on the J604 keeps power-request bit 21 (MSR, the scaler's
report entry) set for the whole of a video decode session: its request
word reads 0x209000 between decode jobs and 0x309000 during them, in a
hypervisor trace of 4K HEVC, H.264 and AV1 decode. Our AVD raises only
bit 20, so its request word is 0x100000 while decoding.

Make the scaler's report entry a second parent of the AVD's, so bit 21
rises with the decoder and falls when it idles, as on macOS.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604-lab.dtsi | 8 +++++++-
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604-lab.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604-lab.dtsi
index 1f2f975f29..c93dc4122a 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604-lab.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604-lab.dtsi
@@ -1453,7 +1453,13 @@ pmp_report_avd_sys: report@14 {
 		reg = <0x14>;
 		label = "pmp-avd-sys";
 		#power-domain-cells = <0>;
-		power-domains = <&ps_avd_sys>;
+		/*
+		 * macOS also holds the scaler's request bit (21) for the whole
+		 * decode session: its request word is 0x209000 between jobs and
+		 * 0x309000 during them. pmp-msr as a second parent raises it
+		 * with the AVD and drops it when the AVD idles.
+		 */
+		power-domains = <&ps_avd_sys>, <&pmp_report_msr>;
 		apple,dvfs = <418 2>;
 		apple,no-ack;
 	};
